cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tem1-allosteric-design: multi-generator de novo design against the TEM-1 beta-lactamase allosteric pocket"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Sutanu"
    family-names: "Mukhopadhyay"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8243-2138"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mukherjeesutanu/tem1-allosteric-design"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - de-novo-design
  - allosteric-inhibitor
  - beta-lactamase
  - molecular-docking
  - generative-chemistry
  - structure-based-drug-design
abstract: >
  A reproducible pipeline that designs candidate ligands for the validated
  allosteric pocket of TEM-1 beta-lactamase (PDB 1PZO, 1PZP) using three
  different generative paradigms - knowledge-based fragment replacement
  (CReM), evolutionary SELFIES search, and a pretrained SAFE-GPT sequence
  model - and triages them with a docking protocol that is validated by
  redocking before use, plus selectivity, site-specificity and
  interaction-fingerprint controls. No compound is experimentally validated.
